# DJ Library Tools

Cross-platform Python CLI to manage the **Master** DJ music library on NAS and sync to Serato/Rekordbox.

**Source of truth:** AGENT_HANDOFF.md, PM_PLAN.md, TEST_PLAN.md, TECH_DEBT.md, RISKS.md, RELEASE.md, INCIDENTS.md; `.cursor/skills/` (see [.cursor/skills/README.md](.cursor/skills/README.md)).

**SDD — no PRs:** Pull requests are **not raised**. Pre-commit review is the **agent pod consensus** — see [.cursor/rules/pre-commit-gate.mdc](.cursor/rules/pre-commit-gate.mdc). Before commit: tester (pytest green) → code-reviewer → code-quality-gate → tech-debt-evaluator → security-reviewer when relevant.

**Operating model:** green-and-clean (scope); context-bootstrapper (start/resume); session-summarizer (handoff).

**TDD:** TEST_TDD.md + tester skill; Tier 1 = `python -m pytest -q`.

**Merge-ready:** `python -m pytest -q` — run before commit; same gate as CI.

**Git:** github-feature-workflow skill — feature branch → pod consensus → commit → merge/push to `main` (no PR).

**Safety:** Master is source of truth. Never delete from Master without explicit user approval.

**Handoff:** handoff-checklist.mdc when user wants a handoff.

**Upstream:** Tracks [AgenticTemplate](https://github.com/pbuckles22/AgenticTemplate) — `git fetch upstream && git merge upstream/main` for shared skills/rules. **Epic close:** when an epic's in-scope work is done, run pm-governance *Epic close* automatically (includes `handoff-checklist.mdc`) � do not wait for the user to ask (`.cursor/rules/epic-close.mdc`).
